/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Example_AnalysisLevels Levels
 * @ingroup DspCore_Examples_Analysis
 * @brief Measure block peak and RMS levels safely.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_AnalysisLevels_Goal Goal
 * Calculate peak and RMS for a compact signal, then confirm that the RMS scale
 * stays finite for the largest representable input.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_AnalysisLevels_Run Run
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/DspCore_Analysis_Levels_d
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_AnalysisLevels_Output Output
 * @code{.text}
 * Input [-3,4,0,0]: peak=4; expected=4
 * RMS=25/10; expected=25/10
 * Maximum finite input: scaled RMS stays finite: PASS
 * Overall: PASS
 * @endcode
 *
 * The signal has a peak of four and RMS of 2.5. The final line demonstrates
 * that the implementation scales before squaring instead of overflowing.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_AnalysisLevels_Code Implementation
 * \include Analysis/Levels/Shared.cpp
 */
